File List
=========
File List for Ports.zip:

Coastrir.txt - This file - For information - Need not be copied to PSION
Coastrir.pic - Icon File - Place in *:\APP\MAPPERIR\
Coastrir.mp3 - Overlay Datafile for Mapper 3.3 - Place in *:\APP\MAPPERIR\
Coastrir.dbf - Database of Station frequencies and channels - Place in *:\DAT\

Description of Overlay
======================
This overlay lists all 13 Department of the Marine Coast Radio stations in Eire through which ships may link call STD numbers anywhere in the World and vice-versa using VHF/MF Maritime Radio.  There is no HF service in Eire.

The Overlay includes a Database file which contains all station channel and frequency information as well as times for Traffic Lists, Navigation Warnings, Weather Forecasts and Gale Warnings.

Intention of Overlay
====================
The overlay assists in the location of the nearest coast radio station for those at sea.  For those ashore it assists in the identification of the nearest station to a vessel through which you can ask for traffic to the vessel to be routed.  To place a call to a ship  through any of these stations call (from UK) (01) 01 785444.  The Department of the Marine will assist in the whole process and direct your call through the correct station.

The Mapper overlay offers the following information:
====================================================
A yacht transmitting to a radio mast Icon shows the location of the station aerials.
The first field gives the NAME OF THE STATION
The second field gives the keystroke that will search the database file for the station information.

The NAME OF THE STATION is the name which the radio station officers will respond to when called by ships.  This name will almost certainly differ from the name of the nearest geographical town.  Maritime Radio station names usually reflect the name of the sea area they serve or the name of the nearest coastal feature where the aerials are located.  

The Reference field gives the keystroke that looks up the DATA application to find the full station listing.  Full instructions as to how to use this feature are given in the Mapper help file but in summary:

- Install the database on any drive and open it using the DATA button

- Press the SYSTEM button

- Move to Mapper and start it.

- Use MENU - FIND - FIND IN OVERLAY to locate your station choice (Hot Key - Psion Y)

- Use MENU - TOWNS/ITEMS - Search in DATA for ........... (No Hot Key)

The correct DATA file must be open in order for the search to work correctly.

NAVIGATION WARNINGS
===================
- Absolutely no liability can be or will be accepted for accidents caused by using this information whilst at sea.  This information does not replace officially recognised navigational information required to be carried aboard your vessel by the resolutions of the International Maritime Organisation as enacted by the UK MERCHANT SHIPPING (NAVIGATION PUBLICATIONS) REGULATIONS 1972 (as amended or may be amended).

- You are reminded that Mapper calculates distances in Statute Miles and not in Nautical Miles.  For comparision 1 Nautical Mile equals approximately 1.14 Statute miles.

